:"T"},{"type":"text","text":" to be stored must be a trivial type. The memory"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"must also be uninitialized, initialized to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":", or initialized to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another trivial type that is layout compatible with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storeBytes(of:toByteOffset:as:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the memory is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initialized to the raw bytes of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"type":"text","text":". If the memory is bound to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U"},{"type":"text","text":" that is layout compatible with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":", then it contains a value of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U"},{"type":"text","text":". Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storeBytes(of:toByteOffset:as:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not change the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound type of the memory."}]},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A trivial type can be copied with just a bit-for-bit copy without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any indirection or reference-counting operations. Generally, native"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Swift types that do not contain strong or weak references or other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forms of indirection are trivial, as are imported C structs and enums."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need to store into memory a copy of a value of a type that 